# 4. Paytm Mobile Recharge – System Integrations

The main integrations involved in a mobile recharge flow are:

| Integration Point       | Test Case                                                  | Expected Result                                                                        |
| ----------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **User Login**          | Log in using valid Paytm credentials.                      | User should be authenticated and taken to the account/home page.                       |
| **Mobile Number**       | Enter a valid mobile number for recharge.                  | The number should be accepted and the relevant recharge options should be shown.       |
| **Plan Selection**      | Select an available recharge plan.                         | Correct plan amount, validity and benefits should be displayed.                        |
| **Payment Gateway**     | Select a payment method and complete the payment.          | Payment should be processed and the recharge should be successful.                     |
| **Recharge System**     | Verify the recharge status after successful payment.       | Recharge should be marked as successful for the selected number.                       |
| **SMS/Notification**    | Complete a successful recharge and check for confirmation. | A recharge confirmation notification/SMS should be generated with the correct details. |
| **Transaction History** | Open transaction/recharge history after the recharge.      | The latest recharge should appear with the correct amount and status.                  |

### Final Conclusion

The Paytm recharge process depends on several systems working together. Testing each integration point helps ensure that **login, recharge plans, payment, recharge processing, notifications and transaction history** all work correctly as one complete flow.
